<div class="not-prose">
<p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-6">After a crash in Spokane, safety comes first and the tow comes second. If anyone is hurt, or a vehicle is blocking traffic and cannot be moved, <strong class="text-white">call 911</strong>. Once everyone is safe and police (if called) say the vehicle can go, call <strong class="text-white">(509) 797-7999</strong> and we will connect you with a local partner tow company, 24/7.</p><h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-14 mb-5 pt-10 border-t border-slate-800">What to do after a car accident, in order</h2><ol class="space-y-4 my-6"><li class="flex gap-4"><span class="shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-full border border-red-500/50 text-red-400 text-sm font-bold">1</span><div class="pt-1"><p class="font-semibold text-white">Check for injuries and call 911 if needed.</p></div></li><li class="flex gap-4"><span class="shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-full border border-red-500/50 text-red-400 text-sm font-bold">2</span><div class="pt-1"><p class="font-semibold text-white">Get out of traffic if you safely can.</p><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mt-1">Washington’s &quot;Steer It, Clear It&quot; rule asks drivers in minor, no-injury crashes to move their cars out of travel lanes when it is safe. On I-90, US-195 or US-2, stay well off the road behind a barrier if possible.</p></div></li><li class="flex gap-4"><span class="shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-full border border-red-500/50 text-red-400 text-sm font-bold">3</span><div class="pt-1"><p class="font-semibold text-white">Turn on hazards and set out flares or triangles</p><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mt-1">if you have them, especially at night or in snow.</p></div></li><li class="flex gap-4"><span class="shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-full border border-red-500/50 text-red-400 text-sm font-bold">4</span><div class="pt-1"><p class="font-semibold text-white">Exchange information</p><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mt-1">Names, phone numbers, insurance, plates. Take photos of all vehicles, the scene and road conditions.</p></div></li><li class="flex gap-4"><span class="shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-full border border-red-500/50 text-red-400 text-sm font-bold">5</span><div class="pt-1"><p class="font-semibold text-white">Decide if the car can be driven.</p><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mt-1">Leaking fluids, a wheel that is bent or will not turn, airbags deployed, lights broken at night, or a hood that will not latch are all good reasons to tow it.</p></div></li><li class="flex gap-4"><span class="shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-full border border-red-500/50 text-red-400 text-sm font-bold">6</span><div class="pt-1"><p class="font-semibold text-white">Call for a tow</p><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mt-1">and tell the dispatcher what is damaged so the right truck comes.</p></div></li></ol><h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-14 mb-5 pt-10 border-t border-slate-800">When police call the tow</h2><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">If police respond and your vehicle is disabled or blocking the road, the officer may arrange the tow. In that case the car goes to the tow company the officer calls, and you deal with that company directly. If you later need to find where it went, see <a class="text-red-500 font-semibold hover:underline" href="/towed-car-spokane">car towed in Spokane: how to find it</a>. If the officer lets you choose, you can call us for a tow to the shop or home you pick.</p><h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-14 mb-5 pt-10 border-t border-slate-800">Where should the car go?</h2><div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 my-6"><div class="border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-5"><p class="font-semibold text-white mb-1">Your body shop or mechanic.</p><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">Best if you already have one. It avoids a second tow later.</p></div><div class="border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-5"><p class="font-semibold text-white mb-1">Your home.</p><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">Fine if you have room and want time to talk with your insurer before choosing a shop.</p></div><div class="border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-5"><p class="font-semibold text-white mb-1">A shop your insurer suggests.</p><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">Ask your claim adjuster; some insurers have preferred shops.</p></div></div><div class="bg-slate-900/70 border border-slate-800 border-l-4 border-l-amber-500/70 rounded-lg p-5 my-6 text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">Try to avoid having the car taken to a storage yard if you do not have to. Storage fees can add up daily while a claim is open.</div><div class="my-12 border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/70 rounded-xl p-6 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4"><div class="text-center sm:text-left"><p class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">Need a tow after a crash?</p><p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">24/7. Price confirmed on the phone before a truck is sent.</p></div><a href="tel:+15097977999" class="shrink-0 bg-gradient-to-r from-red-600 to-red-700 text-white px-6 py-3 rounded-xl hover:from-red-700 hover:to-red-800 transition font-semibold flex items-center gap-2"><svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M3 5a2 2 0 012-2h3.28a1 1 0 01.948.684l1.498 4.493a1 1 0 01-.502 1.21l-2.257 1.13a11.042 11.042 0 005.516 5.516l1.13-2.257a1 1 0 011.21-.502l4.493 1.498a1 1 0 01.684.949V19a2 2 0 01-2 2h-1C9.716 21 3 14.284 3 6V5z"></path></svg><span>(509) 797-7999</span></a></div><h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-0 mb-5 pt-10 border-t border-slate-800">What accident towing costs</h2><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">A straightforward tow of a damaged car that still rolls is estimated the same way as any other tow: a <strong class="text-white">$140 hook fee plus $6 per mile, with a $200 minimum</strong>. Wheels that will not roll, a car off the road, a rollover, or debris cleanup can add to the price; those are quoted on the phone before a truck is sent. See <a class="text-red-500 font-semibold hover:underline" href="/towing-cost-spokane">Spokane towing cost</a> for worked examples.</p><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">Damaged cars usually go on a <a class="text-red-500 font-semibold hover:underline" href="/flatbed-towing">flatbed</a>, which carries the whole vehicle and is gentler on bent suspension and AWD drivetrains. If the car slid into a ditch or snowbank, it needs a <a class="text-red-500 font-semibold hover:underline" href="/winch-out-recovery">winch-out</a> first. For a truck, RV or commercial vehicle, see <a class="text-red-500 font-semibold hover:underline" href="/heavy-duty-towing">heavy duty towing</a>.</p><h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-14 mb-5 pt-10 border-t border-slate-800">Insurance and paperwork</h2><ul class="space-y-2 my-6"><li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="shrink-0 mt-1 text-red-400"><svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg></span><span class="text-gray-300">Call your insurer as soon as you can. Collision coverage often pays for towing after an accident, and if the other driver is at fault, their insurer may pay.</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="shrink-0 mt-1 text-red-400"><svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg></span><span class="text-gray-300">Keep the itemized tow receipt and write down where the car was taken.</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="shrink-0 mt-1 text-red-400"><svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg></span><span class="text-gray-300">Washington drivers may also need to file a collision report with the state for crashes with injuries or significant property damage. Check with WSP or your insurer about whether yours qualifies.</span></li></ul><h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-14 mb-5 pt-10 border-t border-slate-800">Accident-prone spots around Spokane</h2><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">Winter is when calls pick up most: black ice on the Latah Creek bridge and Sunset Hill on I-90, the Maple and Monroe hills, US-195 south of town, and the curves on Highway 2 toward Deer Park. Rear-end crashes in stop-and-go traffic on Division Street and the I-90 Thor/Freya interchange area are common year-round.</p><div class="bg-slate-900/70 border border-slate-800 border-l-4 border-l-red-500/60 rounded-lg p-5 my-6 text-gray-300 leading-relaxed"><p class="font-semibold text-white mb-1">Winter tip</p>Leave extra space, and keep a charged phone, a blanket and flares in the car from November to March.</div><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">For all other help across the region, see <a class="text-red-500 font-semibold hover:underline" href="/spokane-towing-services">Spokane towing services</a> or <a class="text-red-500 font-semibold hover:underline" href="/24-hour-towing">24 hour towing</a>.</p><h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-14 mb-5 pt-10 border-t border-slate-800">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><div class="divide-y divide-slate-800 border-y border-slate-800"><div class="py-5"><h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2">Who do I call for a tow after an accident in Spokane?</h3><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">If anyone is hurt or a vehicle is blocking traffic, call 911 first. Once it is safe and police (if present) have cleared the vehicle, call (509) 797-7999 and we will connect you with a local partner tow company, 24/7.</p></div><div class="py-5"><h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2">How much does accident towing cost in Spokane?</h3><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">A normal tow of a damaged car that still rolls is estimated at a $140 hook fee plus $6 per mile, with a $200 minimum. Cars that will not roll, are off the road, or need cleanup are quoted separately, and the price is confirmed before dispatch.</p></div><div class="py-5"><h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2">Will my insurance pay for the tow after a crash?</h3><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">Often, yes. Collision coverage commonly pays for towing after an accident, and the at-fault driver’s insurer may cover it. Policies differ, so call your insurer and keep the itemized receipt.</p></div><div class="py-5"><h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2">Can I choose my own tow company after an accident?</h3><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">Usually, if your vehicle is not blocking traffic and police do not need it moved immediately. If the officer arranges the tow, the car goes with the company the officer called.</p></div><div class="py-5"><h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2">Where should my car be towed after an accident?</h3><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">Ideally straight to the body shop or mechanic that will repair it, or to your home. That avoids a second tow and daily storage fees while your claim is open.</p></div></div><div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-red-600 to-red-700 rounded-2xl p-8 text-center mt-12"><h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-white">Need a Tow After a Crash?</h3><p class="mb-6 text-white/90">Call 24/7. We connect you with a local partner tow company and confirm the price first.</p><a href="tel:+15097977999" class="bg-white text-red-600 px-8 py-4 rounded-xl hover:bg-gray-100 transition font-bold text-lg inline-block shadow-lg">Call (509) 797-7999</a></div>
